# What Prettier does not format, and why each entry is here rather than being a
# gap someone fills later.
#
# The rule this file implements: one formatter per file type. A file that two
# formatters claim is a file that is unformatted by both, because each undoes the
# other on the next save.

# Rust is rustfmt's, configured by rustfmt.toml at the root.
*.rs

# The compiled-script sources are inputs pinned to what a page received.
# `Crate/ChatDriver/Test/Fixture/Expression.json` records the exact bytes, and a
# test compares the compiled output against it - so reformatting these files
# changes the thing under test. The test's own doc calls itself "the assertion
# that rules out a formatter"; leaving prettier in scope would make that
# assertion fire on every run, and re-recording the fixture instead would make it
# tautological.
Crate/*/Source/Script/

# TOML has its own layout rules and rustfmt/prettier disagree about arrays.
*.toml

# Lockfiles are generated; reformatting them is a diff with no meaning.
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
Cargo.lock

# Build output and installed dependencies.
Target/
**/Target/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# The record: research captures, review bundles and the tooling that made them.
# Formatting a capture changes what the page said.
.hermes/

# Generated or vendored trees, if either appears later.
**/Generated/
**/.generated/
**/gen/
vendor/
